  "narrative": {
    "intro": "This ranking shows federal contracts with periods of performance ending within the next 12 months and the total contract values tied to those expirations. Total obligations for contracts with end dates in the next 12 months equal $237B. NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC has $43.2B in expiring contract value. THE BOEING COMPANY appears three times with $32B, $18.1B, and $7.5B in expiring contract value. LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC has $20.6B in expiring contract value. Other large expirations include BELL BOEING JOINT PROJECT OFFICE with $7B, CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC. with $6.7B, SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION with $6B, NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION with $5.4B, and BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION with $5B. Expiring contract value is concentrated in the 12 months ahead: Jul-Sep 2026 has $9.2B, Oct-Dec 2026 has $43.6B, Jan-Mar 2027 has $47.7B, Apr-Jun 2027 has $83B, and Jul-Sep 2027 has $53.9B. Use these figures to watch upcoming recompetes and timing windows for capture work.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which large federal contracts are expiring by September 2027?",
        "body": "NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC has $43.2B in expiring contract value. THE BOEING COMPANY has $32B, $18.1B, and $7.5B in separate expiring contract values. LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC has $20.6B and BELL BOEING JOINT PROJECT OFFICE has $7B in expiring contract value. SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION, CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC., NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION, and BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION have $6B, $6.7B, $5.4B, and $5B respectively in expiring contract value."
      },
      {
        "heading": "When do those expiring contracts end during the next 12 months?",
        "body": "Jul-Sep 2026 has $9.2B in expiring contract value. Oct-Dec 2026 has $43.6B and Jan-Mar 2027 has $47.7B in expiring contract value. Apr-Jun 2027 has $83B and Jul-Sep 2027 has $53.9B in expiring contract value."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Which large federal contracts are expiring soon?",
      "a": "Large federal contracts expiring soon include NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC with $43.2B and multiple THE BOEING COMPANY contracts with $32B, $18.1B, and $7.5B. LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC has $20.6B in expiring contract value. Other notable expirations include BELL BOEING JOINT PROJECT OFFICE with $7B, CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC. with $6.7B, SIKORSKY AIRCRAFT CORPORATION with $6B, NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION with $5.4B, and BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION with $5B."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is a contract recompete?",
      "a": "A contract recompete is the competitive process that occurs when an existing contract’s period of performance ends and the government solicits offers for the next award period. Recompetes can be full and open competitions or set aside for specific small business categories depending on the agency’s acquisition strategy and requirements. Planning ahead for a recompete means tracking the expiring contract’s end date and the agency’s likely procurement approach."
    },
    {
      "q": "How current is this recompete data?",
      "a": "This recompete data covers FY2026 to date. The note states that award value figures are total contract values for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months and that end dates can be extended by options and modifications."
    }
  ],
